==Strategy==
This is a fairly simple yet difficult level; and usually your first introduction to [[Wave Attack]]s. The best way to defeat this stage is to stack ranged attackers at the beginning of the stage to accumulate enough DPS to knock the Crazed Gross Cats back before they are even able to land a hit. Remember to not use meatshields during this stage, as the Crazed Gross Cats can hit a meatshield and trigger a wave that will decimate your stack. If one has a unit with the [[Wave Shield|Wave Blocker]] ability, such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], the stage becomes trivial, since the only difficult part of the stage are the waves produced by the Crazed Gross Cats. 

If you have [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], this stage also becomes a joke, as he'll endlessly knockback the Crazed Gross Cats before they can attack. However, this option is only possible if you have already beaten [[Into the Future]] chapter 3. [[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed UFO Cat]] also makes this stage a cakewalk, due to its high range and [[Wave Immunity]].

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST Units]]: Due to them all possessing [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless]] abilities, the Ubers here can make the stage incredibly easy. [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Shadow Gao]] and [[Iz the Dancer of Grief (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Dancer of Grief]] are especially noteworthy, as not only do they deal [[Massive Damage]] to [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless Enemies]], but they are also immune to [[Wave Attack]]s; without these waves, the Crazed Grosses are horribly outranged.

